Description:

LIST with RETURN (STATUS ...) now returns STATUS data only for mailboxes on
which the user holds the "r" right.  A mailbox the user cannot read is
reported with the \NoSelect attribute and no STATUS response, as RFC 5819
requires.  A subscribed mailbox on which the user has lost the "l" right is
now listed by LIST (SUBSCRIBED) as \NonExistent, the same as a subscribed
mailbox that has been deleted.  Previously a user who had subscribed to a
mailbox they could not read, as :imapdconf:`allowallsubscribe` permits,
could learn its message count and other status through LIST.


